            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "## Want\n\nFrom https://github.com/neovim/neovim/discussions/41997:\n\n<details open><summary>Click me</summary>\n\n> ```lua\n> -- NOTE: Match <what> in <where> <n> times\n> --\n> -- ```lua\n> -- vim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gm\", function() MultiCursor.multi_operator() end, { desc = \"Match operator\" })\n> -- ```\n> --\n> -- Examples:\n> --   gm<iw><al>  - match <inner word> <around lines> (whole buffer)\n> --   2gm<iw><G>  - match first <2> occurrences of <inner word> up to <EOB>\n> --   gm<iw><10j> - match <inner word> in the next 10 lines\n> --\n> ---@param opts? { pattern?: string, range?: vim.Range, visual?: \"pattern\"|\"range\" }\n> MultiCursor.multi_operator = function(opts)\n> ```\n\n</details>\n\nI want different behavior for the counted operator depending on whether it uses a motion or textobject:\n\n```\n2gm<iw><al> - match **first** <2> occurrences of <inner word> in <around lines> (whole buffer)\n```\n\n```\n2gm<iw><G> - match **next** <2> occurrences of <inner word> up to <EOB>\n```\n\nBy \"next\" I mean match occurrences right after the cursor in the motion direction.\n\nThe API is questionable, but whatever.\n\n## Expect\n\nMaybe `v:motion_type`, and/or something exposed via `CmdAtom`?\n\nP.S. I'm not sure if this feature makes sense.",
